// `true | _` covers the whole domain, because one of its spellings does. The
// catch-all walk stopped at the or-pattern, so the arm looked like it covered
// only `true` and a total match was called non-exhaustive.
//
// The accepting side of the same rule whose refusing side is
// `match_or_duplicate_spelling` - a coverage reader that walks an or-list has to
// get both directions right, and one fixture can only show one of them.
fn pick(b: bool) -> int {
    return match b { true | _ => 5 };
}

fn main() {
    println(pick(true));
    println(pick(false));
}
